    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Solves two zero-sum games as linear programs: rock-paper-scissors, whose optimal strategy is uniform with value zero, and a lopsided variant in which the row player&#x27;s rock beats scissors for double stakes, which tilts the game in the row player&#x27;s favour. In every game, the row player&#x27;s guaranteed payoff equals the column player&#x27;s guaranteed loss.">

